            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The address is still working. Wait a moment and try again."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "assistant.explanation" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The address is any OpenAI-compatible base, such as https://api.openai.com/v1, http://localhost:11434/v1, or https://host/v1. Ganit POSTs that base's chat/completions with the one line it could not work out, the model's name, and the Effort you picked, and nothing else: not the rest of the sheet, its title, or anything about this Mac. Effort is how hard the model is asked to think; Medium is the default, Off sends no preference at all and leaves it to the model, and Custom sends a word Ganit does not know, such as minimal. Answers can take a while, and a higher Effort takes longer; the sheet stays editable and shows Asking… until a value arrives, drawn in purple because a model's answer is not a calculation."
          }
        }
      }
    },
